IMPORT prelude

-- Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library, and defines no YMD. The Act counts in hours ("expires 24 hours after it is made",
-- s 147; those are asked as hours and need no date), in plain days ("expires 28 days after it is made, beginning on and
-- including the day the order was made", s 183; "within 28 days after ... beginning on and including the day the order
-- was varied", s 204(1); "within 7 days", s 176), in months ("must not exceed ... 6 months", s 193; "12 months after the
-- matter occurred", s 434(1)) and in business days (ss 73, 74, 76, 90, 97, 124, 191, 226, 373, 374, 380, 383).
--
-- "Business day" is not defined in the Act; the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (not deposited) defines it as a
-- day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday (or bank holiday) in the place concerned. Weekends are worked
-- out here; Victorian public holidays are not in the deposited text, so the questions ask how many fall on weekdays in
-- the period, and the period is lengthened by that many business days (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Mental Health
-- and Wellbeing Act 2022, Version No. 010 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- A number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The day after a day.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS 1)

-- The day before a day.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day before` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` MINUS 1)

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month a number of months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (31 August 2026 plus 6
-- months is 28 February 2027; fork F3 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

§§ `Business days`

-- The day of the week: DATE_SERIAL modulo 7 is 1 on a Monday (2 November 2026), so 6 is a Saturday and 0 a Sunday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `falls on a weekend` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7 EQUALS 6
     OR DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7 EQUALS 0

-- The next day after a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next weekday after` `the start` MEANS
    IF (`the day after` `the start`) `falls on a weekend`
    THEN `the next weekday after` (`the day after` `the start`)
    ELSE `the day after` `the start`

-- The previous day before a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the previous weekday before` `the start` MEANS
    IF (`the day before` `the start`) `falls on a weekend`
    THEN `the previous weekday before` (`the day before` `the start`)
    ELSE `the day before` `the start`

-- The day n weekdays after a day (the day itself not counted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`stepping forward` n `weekdays from` `the start` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the start`
    ELSE `stepping forward` (n MINUS 1) `weekdays from` (`the next weekday after` `the start`)

-- The day n weekdays before a day (the day itself not counted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`stepping back` n `weekdays from` `the start` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the start`
    ELSE `stepping back` (n MINUS 1) `weekdays from` (`the previous weekday before` `the start`)

-- The weekdays after the first day, up to and including the second (0 if the second is not later).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekdays after` `the start` `up to` `the end` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the end` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the start`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the end` `falls on a weekend`
         THEN `the weekdays after` `the start` `up to` (`the day before` `the end`)
         ELSE 1 PLUS `the weekdays after` `the start` `up to` (`the day before` `the end`)

-- "within n business days after" a day: the last day is n business days after it, the day itself not counted; each
-- weekday public holiday in the period moves it on one more weekday (fork F2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE, `the weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last of` n `business days after` `the start` `with` `the weekday public holidays` MEANS
    `stepping forward` (n PLUS `the weekday public holidays`) `weekdays from` `the start`

-- "at least n business days before" a day: the latest day that leaves n business days, the later day counted and the
-- earlier day not (fork F4).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the end` IS A DATE, `the weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day` n `business days before` `the end` `with` `the weekday public holidays` MEANS
    `stepping back` (n PLUS `the weekday public holidays`) `weekdays from` `the end`
